			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TNA IMPACT on AMC Results &#8211; 11/12/26 (Final show before Destination X)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/397327-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-12-26-final-show-before-destination-x/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/397327-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-12-26-final-show-before-destination-x/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:38:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/12/26 TNA IMPACT on AMC results]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397327</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Results for this week&#8217;s TNA IMPACT on AMC is courtesy of TNAWrestling.com: TNA Thursday Night iMPACT! on AMC&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/397327-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-12-26-final-show-before-destination-x/">TNA IMPACT on AMC Results &#8211; 11/12/26 (Final show before Destination X)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Results for this week&#8217;s TNA IMPACT on AMC is courtesy of <a href="https://tnawrestling.com/news/tna-thursday-night-impact-on-amc-results-november-12-2026">TNAWrestling.com</a>:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Thursday Night iMPACT! on AMC is on the air from the Dothan Civic Center in Dothan, AL, and Destination X just three days away.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Elayna Black vs. Heather by Elegance &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Elayna drops Heather to the canvas and locks her in a Chokehold. She rebounds off the ropes, flips Heather down, and slams into her with a Back Elbow Strike. Heather pulls the referee into her path, avoids Elayna in the corner, and connects with a Step Up Enzuigiri. She locks Elayna throat-first against the ropes, stomps on her back, and sends her spine-first into the turnbuckles. Heather goes for a cover, and Elayna kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Heather lands multiple kicks on Elayna in the corner, sets her up to drop her, and Elayna counters by rolling her up. Heather kicks out at two, sends Black across the ring, and slams into her with a Moonsault from the second turnbuckle. Heather goes for a cover and Elayna powers out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Heather slams Black head-first into the canvas, and rains down multiple blows onto her. Black backs Heather into the turnbuckles, Heather grabs her by the hair, and drives her down with a Sunset Flip. Elayna counters with a Dropkick, and builds momentum. She slams into Heather with a Kneestrike, drives her down with a Gutwrench, and goes for a cover. Heather kicks out at two, Elayna Stomps onto her, goes for another cover, and Heather kicks out again at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Heather slams down Elayna between the ropes, connects a Spikerana, and goes for a cover. Elayna kicks out at two, and Heather climbs to the top turnbuckle for Hell Above. Elayna avoids her and drives Heather down with Blackout to secure the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Elayna Black Def. Heather by Elegance &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA World Tag Team Champion Ryan Nemeth demands the Director of Authority to find him justice, and Santino announces at Destination X The Nemeths will put their titles on the line against syX, and Moose and Matt Hardy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Director of Operations Daria Rae is interrupted by Brian about the Board of Directors concerns. She thinks Santino is causing the hostile work environment, and is concerned with Hartwell, who is going to be on commentary for TNA Knockouts World Tag Team Champions Apex.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>TNA Knockouts World Tag Team Champions Apex vs. The King Bees (Charity King &amp; Danni Bee) &#8211; Tag Team Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Knockouts World Champion Indi Hartwell joins Tom Hannifan and Matthew Rehwoldt on commentary for this match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Baszler and Danni kick this tag team match off. Shayna backs Danni into the turnbuckles, and Danni lands multiple strikes onto Shayna. Baszler knocks her down with a Strike, and tags in Zoey. Serrano absorbs chops, and retaliates with two chops of her own. She kicks Danni, Suplexes her, and slams her down with a Lariat. She tags in Baszler, who sets Serrano up to drive a knee into Danni, and follows with a boot of her own. She goes for a cover, and Danni kicks out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Baszler tries to prevent a tag, and Danni escapes to tag in King. King meets Serrano and Baszler in the ring. She drives down Baszler with a Suplex, and drives down Serrano. Serrano and Baszler trade kicks onto King, and Baszler drives her down with Greymatter to secure the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>TNA Knockouts World Tag Team Champions Apex Def. The King Bees (Charity King &amp; Danni Bee) &#8211; Tag Team Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Joseph Sawyer and Samuel Shaw are ready for their Triple Threat TNA World Tag Team Championship at Destination X, and are confident they’re going to walk away the new TNA World Tag Team Champions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA International Champion Jason Hotch is a newly focused and fighting champion. He is a two-time TNA International Champion, and Expressions with AJ Francis interrupt. Francis has his eyes on the TNA International Championship, and leaves Hotch with a warning.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Samuel Shaw acc. by Joseph Sawyer (syX) vs. Moose &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, they charge at each other, and trade blows. Moose Chops Shaw, drives a Back Elbow Strike into him, and Shaw responds with a Back Elbow Strike of his own. Moose Dropkicks Shaw, sets up for a Powerbomb, and Shaw prevents it with a Double Shot to his throat.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Moose Pumpkicks Shaw, Chops him, and charges at him in the corner. Shaw avoids him in the corner, and Moose rains down multiple blows. Shaw sends Moose face-first into the top turnbuckle, sets up to send Moose to the outside, and Moose counters by sending Shaw to the outside. Shaw slides into the ring, distracts the referee, and Sawyer attacks Moose.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He climbs back, Shaw connects a boot to drop him, and drives a boot into Moose’s neck. Shaw smashes Moose’s left leg into the apron twice, Moose kicks Shaw away, and sends him into Sawyer. Moose sends Shaw into the steel steps, charges at Shaw, and goes knee-first into the steel steps.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Shaw sends Moose back inside the ring, Elbowdrops onto Moose’s injured leg, and connects multiple blows. He Stomps on Moose’s injured knee twice, goes for a cover, and Moose kicks out at two. Moose fires back with two Chops, charges at him, and Shaw Dropkicks Moose’s left knee.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He Elbowdrops Moose twice, and locks up Moose. Moose fires back, and they trade blows. Shaw drives a knee into Moose’s mid-section, tries to send Moose to the outside, and Moose holds onto the ropes. He slams down Shaw with a Clothesline, sets up to Spear Shaw, but his leg gives out. He Powerbombs Shaw, crushes him with a Senton, and prevents Sawyer from getting involved. Shaw drives him down with a Spinebuster, goes for a cover, and Moose kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Shaw climbs to the top turnbuckle, and Moose charges into him. Moose meets Shaw at the top turnbuckle, and Superplexes Shaw. Sawyer slides a chair into the ring, and Shaw attacks Moose with the steel chair.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Moose Def. Samuel Shaw acc. by Joseph Sawyer (syX) &#8211; Via Disqualification &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matt Hardy rushes to the aid of Moose with a steel pipe in hand. Shaw and Sawyer escape up the ramp.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Knockouts TV Champion M by Elegance is backstage discussing the magazine, and Heather overhears her. M thinks Heather is dragging The Elegance Brand down, and wants Heather to make sure M wins her Knockouts Ultimate X match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>TNA Injury Report Presented by Stranglehold:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>TNA X Division Champion Amazing Red is currently out of action due to neck and head injuries.</li>



<li>Eddie Edwards is experiencing lower back issues after his match with Bear Bronson, and has been cleared to compete.</li>



<li>Jeff Hardy remains out of action after the brutal syX Slaughterhouse match.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Wrestling presents Destination X presented by iHeartRadio, on Sunday, November 15, in Edmonton, Alberta, CAN. Tickets are on-sale now at ticketmaster.com!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA World Tag Team Champion Nic Nemeth is with Director of Authority Santino Marella, and is upset about the TNA World Tag Team Championship at Destination X. Santino states if Nic Nemeth loses tonight against Elijah he will lose his contractual rematch for the TNA World Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Mustafa Ali vs. Frankie Kazarian acc. by Avery Styles &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kazarian and Ali trade early pin attempts, Ali sends Frankie towards the corner, and Kazarian avoids him. He drops Kazarian, goes for a cover, and Kazarian kicks out at two. Kazarian answers with a Low Dropkick into a Side Russian Leg Sweep, goes for a cover, and Ali kicks out at two. He sets up for Chicken Wing, and Ali counters with a Jaw Breaker. Ali charges at Kazarian, he avoids Mustafa, and Ali goes face-first into the turnbuckles. He connects a Back Elbow Strike onto Kazarian, drives him down with a Rolling Neckbreaker, and goes for a cover. Kazarian kicks out at two and Ali locks him in a Chokehold.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kazarian breaks free, Ali drops him with a Neckbreaker into a cover, and Frankie kicks out at two. Mustafa Ali climbs to the top turnbuckle, sets up for the 450, and Kazarian rolls out of the way. He flattens Ali with a Clothesline, lands multiple strikes, and cuts down Ali. Kazarian slams down Ali, crushes him with a Springboard Legdrop, and sets up for Fade to Black.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ali prevents it, Bellclaps Kazarian, and sends him to the outside. Kazarian connects a Guillotine Legdrop through the ropes, he slams Ali down with a Slingshot DDT into a cover, and Ali kicks out at two. Frankie climbs to the top rope, and Ali drags Kazarian into a Cutter. He dives through the ropes to wipe Kazarian out on the outside. He sends Kazarian back into the ring, and shoves Avery down.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As Ali gets back into the ring, Frankie drives him down with a Slingshot Cutter, and Avery jumps onto the edge of the apron. Frankie Kazarian calms down Avery, and Ali rolls up Kazarian to secure the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Mustafa Ali Def. Frankie Kazarian acc. by Avery Styles &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The System is a family, and they are back on track. Cedric Alexander is ready to be one step closer to bringing the TNA X-Division title back.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Righteous welcome Xia Brookside into their flock.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Rock-Solid Moment of the Night presented by Blue Chew is the Superplex from Moose onto Shaw.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Destination Next starts now. Trey Miguel reflects on his childhood, and what it was like growing up for him in Toledo, OH. He’s proud of the person he has become, and his hardships have helped shape him. Trey’s dad views Miguel as a go-getter. His friends and family can see his passion for pro-wrestling.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Countdown to Destination X presented by iHeartRadio starts live and free at 5PM ET streaming across TNA social and digital platforms, as well as TNA+. The Countdown begins with the pair of two 3-way qualifying matches for the World X Cup.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Destination X goes live on TNA+ and PPV.com at 6PM ET, and for the first time ever, there are two Ultimate X matches.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One will determine the #1 Contender for the TNA X-Division Championship between BDE, Joe Alonzo, John Skyler, KC Navarro, Cedric Alexander, and Rich Swann.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The other will determine the future #1 Contender for the TNA Knockouts World Championship between Tasha Steelz, M by Elegance, Xia Brookside, Shotzi Blackheart, Gabby Forza, and Jada Stone.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA World Tag Team Champions The Nemeths face off against syX as well as Moose and Matt Hardy for the TNA World Tag Team Championship in a Triple Threat Match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Knockouts World Champion Indi Hartwell looks to defend her title against one half of the TNA Knockouts World Tag Team Champion Shayna Baszler.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA World Champion Leon Slater takes on Trey Miguel in the main event.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Destination Next continues with TNA World Champion Leon Slater. Winning the TNA World Championship gave him a huge sense of achievement, and that everything has been worth it. He reflects on the weight that comes with being TNA World Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">John Skyler is still torn up about Mila Moore.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Elijah vs. TNA World Tag Team Champion Nic Nemeth &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If Nic Nemeth loses to Elijah, he loses his contractual rematch for the TNA World Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, Nic Nemeth Dropkicks Elijah, drives him down with a Neckbreaker, and Elbowdrops onto him for a cover. Elijah kicks out, and answers with a Clothesline. He chops Nemeth, and drives him face-first into the top turnbuckle. Elijah sends Nic across the ring, climbs to the top rope, and forces Nic Nemeth to Walk with Elijah.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He drives down Nemeth, and Nic Nemeth fires back by sending Elijah face-first into the turnbuckles. Elijah strikes Nic, connects a Knee-Strike between the ropes, and Chops him. He crushes Nic with a Draping DDT, goes for a cover, and Nic kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nic rolls to the outside, Elijah follows suit, and slams Nic head-first into the barricade. Nemeth sends Elijah knee-first into the steel steps, and rolls back into the ring. Elijah catches Nic out of Famouser, spikes him down with a Powerbomb, and goes for a cover. Nic kicks out at two, and rolls to the outside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He follows Nic to the outside, slams Nic against the steel steps, and Nic connects a Headbutt. Elijah Chops Nic again, rolls Nic back into the ring, and follows after. Nic Nemeth fires back with multiple strikes, and Elijah answers with a strike of his own. He stomps Nic’s midsection, rolls to the outside, and looks under the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nic Nemeth attacks him from behind, Elijah chops him against the barricade, and rolls them back into the ring. He hoists Nic onto his shoulders, Nic goes to the eyes of Elijah, and plants Elijah with a DDT into a cover. Elijah kicks out at two, and Nic locks Elijah into a Chokehold.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nemeth drives down Elijah with a Neckbreaker, crushes Elijah in the corner twice, and Elijah counters with a boot to the face of Nic. Elijah plants Nic, and they both go down in the center of the ring. Elijah spikes Nic with a Twisting Suplex into the canvas, goes for a cover, and Nic kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He sets up Nic on the top rope, lands multiple strikes, and Chops him. Elijah meets Nic at the top turnbuckle, drives down Nic with Razors Edge into a cover, and Nic kicks out at two. Elijah sends Nic into the ropes, and Nic uses the top rope to his advantage. Elijah charges at Nic, Nemeth counters with a Superkick, and topples onto Elijah for the cover. Elijah kicks out at two, and Nic Nemeth connects back-to-back Shots to the Heart of Elijah.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nic climbs to the top turnbuckle, Elijah catches him with a Knee-Strike into a cover, and Nic kicks out at two. They trade blows, Nic connects a Superkick, drives Elijah down with Dangerzone, he goes for a cover, and Elijah kicks out at two. Nic connects a Superkick as Elijah tries to get back into the ring, he gets a low blow with the rope onto Elijah, and drives him down with Dangerzone to secure the pinfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>TNA World Tag Team Champion Nic Nemeth Def. Elijah &#8211; Singles Match</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Taryn Terrell and Harley Hudson welcome Mila Moore to the dollhouse&#8230;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA Thursday Night iMPACT! on AMC goes off the air…</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-results/397327-tna-impact-on-amc-results-11-12-26-final-show-before-destination-x/">TNA IMPACT on AMC Results &#8211; 11/12/26 (Final show before Destination X)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
