					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-news/397323-former-tna-champion-reportedly-gone-from-company/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:16:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Contract Update]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Lei Ying Lee]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397323</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>PWInsider has reported that Lei Ying Lee is no longer signed to TNA Wrestling, with Fightful Select confirming&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-news/397323-former-tna-champion-reportedly-gone-from-company/">Former TNA champion reportedly gone from company</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://pwinsider.com/article/213625/former-tna-knockouts-champion-gone-from-promotion.html?p=1">PWInsider</a> has reported that Lei Ying Lee is no longer signed to TNA Wrestling, with Fightful Select confirming the departure.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Lee&#8217;s run with the company saw her win the TNA Knockouts Championship twice in the span of roughly two years.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Notably, sources within TNA stated that an offer was made, but the two sides could not come to an agreement.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Lee last competed for the company in July, being away from recent TNA tapings as she was overseas in China.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">She is expected to continue wrestling, with discussions reportedly going on with other companies as Lee evaluates her future.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-news/397323-former-tna-champion-reportedly-gone-from-company/">Former TNA champion reportedly gone from company</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-news/397323-former-tna-champion-reportedly-gone-from-company/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Report on possible changes to John Cena Classic</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397316-report-on-possible-changes-to-john-cena-classic/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397316-report-on-possible-changes-to-john-cena-classic/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:00:33 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[John Cena]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[John Cena Classic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397316</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Fightful Select reports WWE is looking to get even more talent involved in the John Cena Classic. The&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397316-report-on-possible-changes-to-john-cena-classic/">Report on possible changes to John Cena Classic</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fightful Select reports WWE is looking to get even more talent involved in the John Cena Classic.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report notes that one idea that floated around internally is to feature multi-person matches rather than exclusively traditional singles competition. It was added this proposed new format would allow WWE to showcase additional talent throughout the event, thus potentially giving the opportunity for more talent to participate. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It should be noted, however, there is no confirmation WWE has officially settled on the change, but that it still remains one of the possibilities discussed backstage.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During a <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">previous interview with The Takedown on SI</a>, Cena said the Classic will not feature a bracket-style tournament, as some fans had speculated. It will instead be centered around a series of exhibition matches, much like how it was determined who is final opponent was for his retirement match last December.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the time of this writing, Cody Rhodes and Zilla Fatu are first two participants invited to the John Cena Classic.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The John Cena Classic will take place during a second episode of Monday Night Raw on December 14 at the ESPN Wild World Of Sports Complex at Walt Disney World in Orlando, Florida. The first-ever Cena Classic champion will be awarded a belt that is similar to his old WWE spinner championship belt. Those who are WWE Club Members will get to vote on John Cena Classic participants.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Championship will be that of similarity to Cena&#8217;s old WWE spinner title belt.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397316-report-on-possible-changes-to-john-cena-classic/">Report on possible changes to John Cena Classic</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
